('WF01','Create an individual account','Visitor selects Create account from public Sign in.','Supplied given/family name, exact birth date for product eligibility, email and/or phone, password confirmation, language and notices.','Draft > Submitted > Account active','Applicant;Identity service','Age-policy review complete; unique supported sign-in identity; real successful save; no staff/person record created.','Account holder; security support handles failures.','Under-age applicants use verified guardian-assisted person/event records; ambiguous contacts use neutral recovery. Missing verification remains Unverified, not fake success.','One individual account and own combined home, with skippable profile completion.','S06'),
('WF02','Recover credentials and manage sessions','Account holder chooses Forgot password, Change password or Lost device in My account.','Own identifier, actual verified channel or recorded manual identity review; recovery token; current password for authenticated changes; selected session IDs.','Requested > Identity checked > Recovery authorized > Credentials changed > Other sessions revoked > Closed','Holder;Identity reviewer;Security service;Holder;Session service','A contact challenge must really succeed; office member recovery cannot reset staff; privileged support actor reauthenticates; no secrets in history.','Security support; ordinary office only for eligible nonstaff recovery.','Unknown contact yields neutral response. No usable channel uses reviewed manual recovery. Lost response checks actual reset state; never email an invented password.','Holder can authenticate; revoked sessions fail their next protected request; minimal recovery audit retained.','S06'),
('WF03','Invite and link an existing person','Authorized office selects Invite from a verified, unlinked person.','Person/parish ID, inviting office, intended contact, verification method, seven-day expiry and hash-backed one-use link.','Prepared > Link created > Shared manually or sent > Claimed > Linked','Office;Invitation service;Office/delivery service;Recipient;Identity linker','Office verifies intended person; recipient authenticates, confirms account and association; existing account/person links are rechecked at claim.','Office identity reviewer; recipient owns claim action.','Expired/revoked/wrong-person links stop. Used claim returns existing link for same permitted claimant; conflicts need identity review. Link creation is not delivery.','Exactly one intended account-person association; no ministry/staff grant.','S06 S07'),
('WF04','Follow, join and leave a parish','Signed-in user chooses Follow, Set primary or Request membership on a published parish.','Target parish, relationship request, supplied distinguishing facts and minimal representation/identity evidence.','Membership requested > Under identity review > Linked > Departure requested > Membership ended','User;Office reviewer;Office reviewer;Member;Office reviewer','Following and primary selection are immediate preferences. Membership link requires office identity check; no self-review; departure previews open work.','Parish office, falling back to assigned priest/Parish Admin.','Ambiguous/archive/already-linked candidates wait for evidence. Decline gives useful reason. Leaving/unfollowing does not move records or revoke unrelated appointments.','Dated parish relationship; permitted historical request tracking retained.','S07'),
('WF05','Propose and review official profile corrections','Member opens My parish records and selects Propose correction.','Field ID, original snapshot, proposed value, reason, optional evidence and source revision.','Draft > Submitted > Under review > Partially or fully resolved > Closed','Member;Member;Office reviewer;Office reviewer;Case service','Per-field review; reviewer is not applicant; original/submitted/current values compared; counterproposal needs applicant confirmation when representing their assertion.','Office data reviewer; applicant answers clarification.','Withdraw or replace before decision commits. Stale field requires reconciliation; already-correct value resolves without redundant write. Official register facts use WF19.','Only supported approved fields change; preserved original/proposed/applied values and applicant-visible decision.','S07 S08'),
('WF06','Create, correct, archive and restore a person','Office selects Add person or permitted Edit/Archive/Restore on a person detail.','Parish, supplied name, purpose/source, duplicate checks, known identity/contact facts, precision flags and archive/death evidence.','Provisional > Active > Archive proposed > Archived > Restore reviewed > Active restored','Office;Office reviewer;Office;Data reviewer;Data reviewer;Office reviewer','At least one supplied distinguishing name; unknown dates/scripts allowed provisionally; official-output readiness separate; restore proves same identity.','Office data owner; priest reviews official-identity implications.','Do not invent dates/names. Archive previews rosters, invitations, account links, giving and open work. Death is a reviewed fact; account closure is separate.','Stable person ID, historical links preserved, no automatic reactivation of prior roles or consent.','S08 S10'),
('WF07','Review duplicates, merge and unmerge','Office opens Duplicates or a suggested match from import/intake.','Candidate IDs, evidence, differing fields, surviving values and impact on links/official/financial records.','Candidate > Compared > Merge proposed > Independently reviewed > Merged > Unmerge review > Corrected','Office;Identity reviewer;Office;Independent domain reviewer;Merge operator;Identity reviewer;Authorized operator','Multiple identity signals; explicit survivor; conflicting account links resolved separately; preserve source snapshots and immutable official/financial facts.','Named merge reviewer and office data owner.','Different person dismisses suggestion with evidence. Uncertain stays pending. Later dependencies prevent blind rollback; suspend affected releases for review.','Traceable alias/survivor mapping or reviewed unmerge with every downstream correction accounted for.','S10'),
('WF08','Maintain households, relationships and representation','Office opens household create/join/split/merge/contact change; guardian proposes authority update.','People, primary household, explicit person-to-person relation, shared address/contact, overrides, envelope history and representation scope/evidence.','Draft > Impact reviewed > Saved > Relationship/authority review > Confirmed','Office;Office;Office;Authorized identity reviewer;Reviewer','One primary administrative household; no cycles; household contact does not confer authority; separate guardian/representative permission for each purpose.','Office data owner; safeguarding/privacy reviewer for disputed authority.','Split preserves old gifts, consent, official snapshots and requester identity. Sensitive custody/adoption facts are restricted. Do not duplicate a person to model secondary residence.','Accurate dated relationships and contact defaults, with accessible relationship list and purpose-scoped representation.','S09'),
('WF09','Import reviewed source records','Authorized office/import user selects Import for a specific parish and record class.','Source owner/file/hash/date, mapping, original values, row IDs, preview, errors, duplicate matches and reconciliation totals.','Staged > Mapped > Validated > Domain reviewed > Committed > Reconciled','Importer;Importer;Validation service;Domain reviewer;Importer;Domain reviewer','Whole-file validation first; default atomic import; explicit valid-row-only choice records exclusions. Priest/finance approval for their domain.','Import coordinator and parish domain owners.','Ambiguous dates, missing translations/localities/consent remain unresolved rather than guessed. Retry same source/batch never duplicates rows. Reversal reviews later dependencies.','Committed row ledger, rejected-row report, reconciled source/result totals and source provenance.','S10'),
('WF10','Record historical or external sacramental evidence','Office selects Historical entry or External sacrament reference on a verified person.','Original source parish/country/type/date precision, book/page/number, celebrant, evidence, transcription date and reviewer.','Draft > Source checked > Priest review > Historical entry approved or external reference verified','Office;Source verifier;Assigned priest;Assigned priest','External reference receives no new local celebration number. Historical local numbering follows clergy-approved register policy. Actual entry timestamps are never backdated.','Assigned priest and official-register custodian.','Unknown original facts remain unknown; unverified evidence cannot satisfy final eligibility automatically. Name ambiguity pauses linking, not creates another celebration.','Approved historical local snapshot or verified external reference with clearly different provenance.','S10 S13'),
('WF11','Receive and triage a canonical service request','Guest, unlinked account, member or office-assisted caller selects a supported request type and one parish.','Requester, subject, relationship, origin, contact, service-specific facts, urgency, preferred dates and private/public text separated.','Draft > Received > Triage > Needs information > Ready for decision > Linked office work','Applicant;Applicant/office recorder;Office;Office;Applicant/office;Office','One canonical reference; actual save before receipt; verified representation before disclosure; linked intake and office work share one actionable case identity.','Office queue lead; no-secretary fallback is head priest/appointed office administrator.','Duplicate continues/links existing case; wrong parish returns guidance or reviewed informed reassignment. Withdrawal before handling; later cancellation request.','Stable case/timeline/conversation with exact origin and next responsible actor.','S11'),
('WF12','Complete a general parish service','Applicant chooses Something else, or office classifies a non-sacramental need.','Request narrative, subject/authority, permitted contact, accountable owner, accepted scope and completion evidence.','Received > Needs information > Accepted > In progress > Completed > Closed','Office;Office;Eligible service owner;Assigned worker;Service owner;Office','Acceptance describes what is being done; sensitive pastoral content goes only to eligible clergy; no automatic sacramental/register effect.','Named service owner; office monitors follow-up.','Decline/cancel gives useful reason. Incorrect classification is amended visibly; requester cannot silently edit accepted scope.','Actual service result and applicant-visible completion explanation, with payments/appointments separately linked.','S11 S13'),
('WF13','Reserve a facility','Requester selects free/busy resource and submits a booking request.','Resource, dates/time zone, setup/cleanup, purpose, attendees, responsible adult, equipment, approved prices/deposit terms and access needs.','Draft > Requested > Office reviewed > Tentative hold > Confirmed > In use > Completed','Requester;Requester;Office;Resource manager;Priest or expressly delegated booking approver;Custodian;Custodian','Submission alone holds nothing; hold proposed 24 hours with actual expiry evaluation; confirm rechecks exclusive resources/clergy and approved deposit condition.','Resource manager; priest is default confirmation authority.','Competing request becomes Alternative needed, not auto-refused. Maintenance/schedule changes need reviewed relocation and applicant notices. Cancellation/refund remain separate.','One confirmed reservation/canonical occurrence; custody/access and financial close tasks recorded.','S23'),
('WF14','Baptism preparation, celebration and registration','Applicant/authorized guardian selects Baptism; office may record telephone/in-person intake.','Supplied child/adult identity, date precision, parents/guardian, godparents, external evidence, approved requirement version, date/place/celebrant.','Received > Priest accepted > Preparation > Scheduled > Celebration recorded > Entry submitted > Registered','Office;Assigned priest or instructed secretary;Preparation staff;Scheduling owner;Office/clergy recorder;Office;Assigned priest or instructed secretary','Archived/ambiguous child match resolved; adult/incomplete-parent variants have no impossible required parent field; final requirements and actual celebration verified before register approval.','Responsible priest; preparing office person/team.','Direct priest acceptance skips optional office review only. Missing/illegible evidence returns one item. No-show remains uncelebrated; cancellation before celebration preserves case; registered facts use WF19.','Individual approved register snapshot/number under supplied jurisdiction policy; certificate is a separate request.','S12 S13'),
('WF15','First Communion preparation, celebration and registration','Applicant/guardian or group coordinator starts an individual Communion case.','Identity, verified prior sacrament references where required, formation evidence, individual readiness, shared celebration and approved checklist.','Received > Priest accepted > Formation/preparation > Scheduled > Celebration recorded > Entry submitted > Registered','Office;Assigned priest or instructed secretary;Qualified formation reviewer;Scheduling owner;Office/clergy recorder;Office;Assigned priest or instructed secretary','Actual rite-specific age/prior-record/formation requirements must be supplied; outside-parish evidence is a verified reference; shared event never substitutes for individual readiness.','Assigned priest and formation leader; office coordinates.','Incomplete participant remains pending without blocking unrelated ready candidates. Withdraw/cancel pre-celebration; wrong official facts use WF19.','Separate individual entry and source/formation history, not a group roster treated as proof of reception.','S12 S13'),
('WF16','Confirmation/chrismation preparation and registration','Applicant/office chooses only the jurisdiction-approved separate or baptism-linked option.','Identity, rite/jurisdiction, baptism reference, approved terminology/checklist, sponsor/formation where required, actual celebrant/date.','Received > Rite route verified > Priest accepted > Prepared > Scheduled > Celebrated > Entry approved','Office;Assigned priest;Assigned priest or instructed secretary;Preparation staff;Scheduling owner;Clergy/office recorder;Assigned priest or instructed secretary','Do not infer doctrine or separate ceremonies from a selector. Combined baptism/chrismation shares actual occurrence but keeps approved distinct record references where required.','Competent clergy policy owner and responsible priest.','Unsupported route goes to clergy review. Previously recorded reception is referenced, never duplicated by naming differences. Corrections use WF19.','Only the approved rite route and actual celebration produce an official entry.','S12 S13'),
('WF17','Marriage preparation, celebration and registration','One/both partners or office initiate a marriage request.','Both partners, supplied official names, separate contact/authority, external parish/celebrant, witnesses, prior evidence, special permission references and resources.','Received > Priest review > External/special authorization > Preparation complete > Scheduled > Celebrated > Entry submitted > Registered','Office;Assigned priest;Competent outside/bishop authority;Preparation verifier;Scheduling owner;Clergy/office recorder;Office;Assigned priest or instructed secretary','Special authority is a real unresolved gate when required; outside partner can be external reference; no payment or secretary instruction replaces outside permission.','Assigned priest; competent ecclesiastical authority for exceptional route.','Clergy/room conflicts require alternatives. Partner privacy remains separate. Postponement/cancellation updates linked certificate/booking/payment work; never fabricate a celebration.','Actual reviewed marriage entry with source permissions and immutable issued snapshot.','S12 S13'),
('WF18','Arrange a funeral and record its outcome','Family/representative uses Funeral request plus maintained urgent pastoral contact.','Deceased identity, reported death facts, authorized contact, timing, location, celebrant and approved urgent logistics/checklist.','Received urgent > Priest accepted > Arrangements confirmed > Service occurred > Outcome reviewed > Closed','Office;Assigned priest or instructed secretary;Scheduling owner;Clergy/office recorder;Assigned priest;Office','Funeral is described as a service, not assumed to be a sacrament. No generic formation checklist. Death verification, public naming and account closure are separate reviewed actions.','Duty priest and office funeral coordinator; published out-of-hours availability only.','No claim of continuous monitoring. Uncertain identity/death remains reported. Reschedule/cancel preserves actual logistics and fees; no false service-complete state.','Recorded actual funeral outcome; jurisdiction supplies any register/document requirements; deceased-status review offered separately.','S13'),
('WF19','Correct an approved official entry','Authorized office/priest opens Request official correction from a locked entry.','Original entry/snapshot, disputed fields, source evidence, proposed correction, legal/ecclesiastical authority reference and affected certificates.','Correction drafted > Evidence reviewed > Competent approval > Amendment recorded > Dependent outputs reviewed > Closed','Office;Assigned priest;Competent clergy approver;Register custodian;Signing/release authority;Office','No overwriting registered history or reusing number to hide mistake. Approved amendment preserves original, corrected reading, authority, date and affected version links.','Official register custodian; bishop/competent authority where policy requires.','Wrong-person/uncelebrated record requires restricted substantive review, not ordinary Cancel. Reissue/revoke certificates via WF20/WF21. Exact correction method supplied by authority.','Traceable authorized amendment and reviewed consequences without erasing original.','S12 S14'),
('WF20','Prepare, sign and authorize a certificate','Authorized requester chooses a supported certificate and source entry or planned sacrament.','Subject/requester/authority, purpose, quantity, language/layout, exact official source, approved template and actual signature/seal evidence.','Received > Waiting for official source > Prepared > Priest approved > Priest signed > Bishop accepted > Issued','Office;Source linker;Preparation staff;Assigned priest or instructed secretary;Actual authorized priest signer;Bishop/competent appointed acceptor;Issuance custodian','Waiting state is skipped when exact approved source exists. Proposed default preserves bishop gate for new issues until competent policy changes it. Signing is personal separate authority; final snapshot after applicable gates.','Signing priest; bishop review owner; office preparation lead.','Returned signed content creates new revision, invalidates its material signature and requires resign/review. Legacy issued lacks invented acceptance. No certificate validity period invented.','One versioned issuance authorized by actual applicable signatures/acceptance, ready for separately verified release.','S14'),
('WF21','Release, download or collect an authorized document','Eligible office opens Release reviewed file or Record collection on an authorized issuance.','Exact file/version/language preview, subject, requester, verified recipient/representative, access method, receipt and release expiry.','Prepared private > Recipient verified > Released > Downloaded or physically collected > Receipt confirmed > Closed','Preparation staff;Release verifier;Authorized releaser;Verified recipient/counter staff;Office;Office','Correct certificate/source and all gates; no evidence file selected by default. Sensitive downloads require approved account link or real contact challenge; otherwise office collection.','Named office release verifier; signing authority resolves final-document disputes.','Wrong-file caught before release blocks it. Later withdrawal stops future access and opens restricted disclosure review; downloaded copies cannot be recalled. Tracking alone is not download identity.','Actual release/receipt events, recipient and document version recorded; availability never mislabeled collection.','S14 S15'),
('WF22','Supply and verify evidence','Applicant uploads against a named requirement or office records paper receipt.','Requirement/version, file/type/size/pages, supplier, paper/original receipt, verifier, outcome, expiry/waiver reason.','Missing > Uploaded or paper received > Under review > Verified > Locked with parent','Supplier;Supplier/office;Verifier;Verifier;Parent workflow','Receipt is possession, not verification; exact item due-stage controls readiness; waiver only when competent requirement policy permits.','Requirement verifier and preparing office owner.','Rejected/illegible/expired returns item for replacement; preserve prior version. Partial upload failure retries file only; source-file reuse gets new-purpose/validity check.','Verified/approved-waived checklist with provenance; never automatic clergy approval.','S15'),
('WF23','Maintain a calendar occurrence or recurring series','Authorized office/clergy/leader chooses New event or edits linked source/series.','Owning parish/source, event type, zone, start/end, recurrence/exception, venue/setup, clergy/equipment, audience and public redaction.','Draft > Conflicts checked > Approved source > Published to permitted audience > Occurred > Archived','Editor;Scheduling service;Source approver;Publisher;Event owner;Event owner','Exclusive conflicts block; all recurrence occurrences checked; source workflow owns its approved date/status; no duplicated dates.','Calendar owner and linked source approver.','This occurrence/This and future/Eligible series previews changes. Paid-event material amendments use reconfirm/refund. Private busy intervals never reveal titles/people.','One authoritative occurrence and versioned exception history with correct parish-local time.','S16'),
('WF24','Create and approve an activity/service plan','Coordinator selects linked event then New plan or Copy template.','Event reference, plan version, fixed/relative item times, duration, accountable people, readings/music and audience-specific notes.','Draft > Explicitly saved > Review > Approved running version > Completed > Archived','Coordinator;Coordinator;Reviewer;Priest/operational approver;Coordinator;Coordinator','Final plan fits booked time or approved reschedule; mandatory roles assigned; liturgical content reviewed by priest; source event not silently extended.','One plan coordinator; contributors see only assigned audience.','Unsaved close offers Save/Discard/Stay. Concurrent edits reconcile. Template edits do not mutate saved plans; fixed start constraints shown with gaps/overlaps.','Versioned running sheet and distinct clergy/team/participant prints, no unrelated private notes.','S17'),
('WF25','Maintain music and rights-controlled versions','Authorized librarian chooses Add music, New version or Link to plan.','Supplied title/language, rite/season, key/instruments, lyrics/chords/notes, source, rights/attribution and version.','Draft > Rights/content reviewed > Published resource > Linked version > Withdrawn or archived','Librarian;Rights and clergy reviewer;Resource publisher;Plan coordinator;Resource owner','No printing/downloading/projecting without recorded rights basis. Linking pins a version, not a mutable global body.','Music librarian; designated rights reviewer; priest for religious suitability.','Correction creates version; withdrawal flags future use and preserves lawful past plan record. Unsupported audio hosting is a link, not uploaded playback promise.','Searchable approved version with clear permitted uses and attribution on outputs.','S17'),
('WF26','Apply for ministry membership','Eligible account/person or office selects Apply/Add pending membership on a ministry.','Applicant/person, group, eligibility, consent/trial evidence, capacity and optional applicant message.','Draft > Submitted > Leader reviewed > Priest approved > Active member','Applicant/office;Applicant;Assigned leader;Assigned priest;Roster service','Parish-person link and group eligibility checked; priest may approve directly; office profile checkbox cannot bypass final decision.','Assigned leader then parish priest; no-leader work routes to priest.','Leader decline returns explanation/appeal; conflict uses alternate eligible leader/priest. Pre-review withdraw immediately; post-leader withdrawal uses WF27.','One active roster membership from effective approval, with history separate from leadership access.','S18'),
('WF27','Withdraw an application or privately leave a ministry','Applicant selects Withdraw before membership or Private departure after membership.','Application/membership, requested effect, optional private reason, future commitments/resource handover.','Requested > Priest private review > Approved withdrawal/departure > Roster ended > Follow-up closed','Applicant;Assigned priest;Assigned priest;Roster owner;Handover owner','Before leader approval withdrawal is direct terminal; later request reviewed. Private reason visible only to applicant/authorized parish priests; leaders get neutral end date.','Assigned priest; permitted leader handles neutral operational handover.','User may stop voluntary participation/mute optional messages while review waits. Approval after terminal withdrawal blocked. Outstanding loans/tasks handled without reason disclosure.','Dated end preserves historical attendance and applicant tracking; future rights/assignments reviewed.','S18'),
('WF28','Create meetings and record/correct attendance','Assigned leader opens a group meeting linked to calendar and its date-specific roster.','Meeting occurrence, expected roster snapshot, RSVP, optional restricted reason, attendance state and actual correction reason.','Meeting drafted > Scheduled > Attendance open > Attendance recorded > Period reviewed > Locked','Leader;Calendar owner;Recorder;Recorder;Independent group reviewer;Period owner','Not recorded is not Absent; Present/Late count only under explicit denominator; joins/leaves affect expected-from date, not past facts.','Assigned attendance recorder; monthly reviewer.','Guests are tagged separately; stale cell retry checks revision. Post-close corrections append adjustment with reason. Import preview maps exact person/date/status.','Recorded status per person/meeting and reproducible report with unknown counts.','S19'),
('WF29','Borrow and return group resources','Permitted member/leader selects physical resource request; digital access uses audience directly.','Item/quantity/condition, group owner, borrower/contact basis, due date, issue/return and damage evidence.','Requested > Approved > Issued > Returned > Condition checked > Closed','Borrower;Custodian;Custodian;Borrower/custodian;Custodian;Custodian','Digital files are not physical loans. Available serviceable stock rechecked; departing member keeps limited loan-return route only.','Group/resource custodian.','Overdue/lost/damaged goes to follow-up and WF37 repair/finance as approved. Leader handover transfers custody, never personal notes.','Quantity and condition reconcile with stock; dated loan history and restricted borrower details.','S19'),
('WF30','Offer, confirm and complete volunteer duties','Eligible person opens opportunity or coordinator sends an invitation for a defined slot.','Team/position, time/zone/parish, skills/training/consent, availability, response, replacement and actual hours.','Invited or offered > Awaiting confirmation > Confirmed > Served > Hours submitted > Hours approved','Volunteer/coordinator;Volunteer;Coordinator;Event lead;Volunteer;Independent coordinator','Real overlap and mandatory eligibility block. Other-parish conflict exposes only busy interval. Volunteer remains a member account, not separate login tier.','Volunteer coordinator and event/ministry lead.','Decline invitation directly. Late cancellation/swap leaves vacancy until eligible replacement accepts/confirmed. Drag alternative uses Assign dialog; no false actual hours from schedule.','Confirmed history, actual approved hours and independently accepted replacement when needed.','S20'),
('WF31','Register a participant and manage capacity/consent','Member/guardian/guest or office chooses an eligible event form.','Event/form version, subject/contact/authority, eligibility/age, seat status, consent version, transport, fee snapshot and actual payments.','Draft > Submitted > Reserved or waitlisted > Consent/eligibility reviewed > Confirmed > Registration closed','Applicant;Applicant;Capacity service/office;Consent reviewer;Event approver;Event lead','Event/currency locked after first participant; reserved and confirmed seats consume capacity atomically; unknown age waits review; required consent before confirmation/check-in.','Event registration lead; guardian/participant supplies valid consent.','Concurrent final place gives one reservation, other waitlisted. Waitlist invitation proposed 48h with real expiry task. Reconsent after material change; fee policy/refund separate.','One eligible confirmed participant/transport allocation or clear waiting/cancelled outcome without fictitious payment.','S21'),
('WF32','Publish trilingual public/member/group content','Authorized editor chooses Public website/Announcement then creates or changes a draft.','Audience, revision, EN/FR/AR text, media rights/alt/captions, publishing authority and actual schedule/expiry.','Draft > Awaiting review > Approved > Published > Unpublished or expired > Archived','Editor;Editor;Publisher/domain reviewer;Publisher or real runner;Publisher/real runner;Content owner','All required translations reviewed; exact preview; Save draft never unpublishes last approved live version; organization/title facts retain competent authority.','Appointed content publisher; head priest for parish correctness.','Returned draft leaves live version intact; concurrency compares versions. Accidental privacy publication triggers immediate withdrawal/access revocation and restricted review.','Single published revision with audience, approvals and version history; scheduled task labeled manual if no runner.','S05'),
('WF33','Record and allocate an actual receipt','Authorized cashier/event/finance operator records genuine cash/bank/OMT receipt or claimed transfer awaiting verification.','Payer, original currency/amount/date/method/reference, source case, allocations, exchange basis if actually converted and operator.','Claim reported > Receipt verified > Transaction posted > Allocated > Receipt acknowledged','Payer/office;Finance verifier;Ledger service;Finance allocator;Cashier','Claimed payment is not receipt. One canonical movement ID; allocation sum cannot exceed posted net amount; separate currencies; no duplicate event/Finance receipt.','Finance operator and independent reviewer for corrections.','Overpayment remains unapplied credit/refund task; split participants use explicit allocation; repeated import/retry deduplicates source reference. Corrections reverse, not overwrite.','Posted amount reconciles to allocations plus unapplied remainder; purpose screens show the same movement.','S21 S25'),
('WF34','Check a participant into the exact event','Assigned door operator selects event/occurrence/site and searches authorized registration.','Participant/registration, consent/eligibility, permitted alerts, arrival time, operator and active session.','Expected > Identity checked > Checked in > Checked out > Reentered','Operator;Operator;Operator;Pickup-authorized operator;Operator','Confirmation and required consent valid; duplicate active arrival blocked; independent departure/collector checks use WF58. No individual Mass attendance.','Named event check-in lead.','Walk-in uses WF31 first; unknown age/missing required consent blocks entry until approved supervision procedure resolves it. Offline paper follows WF58 and later reconciliation.','Append-only arrival/exit events and exact currently-present event roster.','S22'),
('WF35','Record and review an incident','Authorized event staff records factual report for a selected event/location/person or an explicitly unlinked parish incident.','Initial facts/time/source, immediate real response, involved IDs, restricted evidence, handlers and guardian-disclosure decision.','Recorded > Triaged > Assigned > Follow-up > Resolved > Closed','Reporter;Safeguarding lead;Independent handler;Handler;Reviewer;Reviewer','Need-to-know field access; no general office count; guardian notice contains own permitted facts only; actual escalation contacts supplied before operation.','Event safeguarding lead and qualified independent incident reviewer.','Immediate action follows real approved procedure. Historical reports never receive invented event links. Amendments preserve initial facts; conflict escalates outside implicated authority.','Restricted incident history with actual actions/follow-up, not a claim emergency broadcasts were delivered.','S22'),
('WF36','Block maintenance and restore safe availability','Resource operator reports issue or requests maintenance period.','Resource/time/setup, severity, existing holds/bookings, relocation plan, assignee, repair evidence/cost and clearance.','Reported > Impact triaged > Block authorized > Repair in progress > Clearance reviewed > Available','Reporter;Resource lead;Resource lead;Repair assignee;Qualified clearance reviewer;Resource lead','Routine work cannot silently displace confirmed bookings. Urgent unsafe resource becomes unavailable immediately with attributed emergency action and prompt review/relocation.','Resource/maintenance lead and competent clearance reviewer.','Notify affected applicants via working channels; unresolved alternatives remain assigned. Repair cost uses financial workflow; reporter cannot claim qualified clearance without authority.','Actual safe restoration date/evidence, repaired quantity and updated linked availability.','S23'),
('WF37','Reserve, issue and reconcile equipment','Requester/custodian adds equipment to a booking or starts a standalone loan.','Stock/serial, serviceable quantity, overlapping commitments, borrower, issue/due, returned quantity/condition and deposit terms.','Requested > Stock reserved > Issued > Return recorded > Damage/loss reviewed > Closed','Requester;Custodian;Custodian;Custodian;Resource reviewer;Custodian','Room-plus-equipment reservation commits together or neither; damaged/unusable stock excluded; no quantity overcommit; financial damage decision separate from condition fact.','Equipment custodian and resource manager.','Partial returns keep outstanding balance. Damage opens WF36 and flags later bookings for alternatives; deposit deductions need approved evidence/refund policy.','Stock = serviceable available + committed/issued + unavailable with traceable movement history.','S23'),
('WF38','Appoint, review, suspend or revoke scoped access','Eligible appointing authority opens Accounts & access at explicit system/diocese/parish/ministry scope.','Verified account, role/title eligibility, local person where needed, grant scope, dates, lead flag, acceptance, reason and approver.','Proposed > Invited > Accepted > Scheduled > Active > Ended or revoked','Appointer;Appointer;Appointee;Appointment service;Appointment service;Eligible authority','Both acceptance/effective time for invited grant; hierarchy enforced; current-password checks for protected changes; priest qualification/title separate. Expiry evaluated at protected requests, not only reminders.','Scope-appropriate appointing authority; bishop controls clergy matters.','No peer/superior escalation. First privileged setup has controlled exception to impossible second-approver prerequisite. Revocation stops next protected access and routes work to eligible replacements.','Scoped dated assignment and immutable history; unrelated account/membership grants survive.','S02 S29'),
('WF39','Create, activate, deactivate or close a parish','Bishop or expressly authorized preparation administrator opens New parish.','Approved identities/jurisdiction, locality, head priest/adoption, trilingual core labels, real office contact and optional secretary.','Private setup draft > Readiness checked > Bishop approved > Created and active > Deactivated > Reactivated or closed','Preparatory admin;Setup reviewer;Bishop;Authorized creator;Eligible authority;Competent authority','Create and activate is one effective action after valid minimum setup; optional gallery/history/import do not add hidden activation gate. Priest authority never derives from admin rank.','Bishop and head priest; Super Admin handles platform setup.','No secretary is normal. No real records permits reviewed setup deletion; record-bearing parish closes/archives, not cascade delete. Higher suspension cannot be overruled by lower role.','Correct public parish and operational scope or explicit closed/status/contact/history access with handover.','S02 S29'),
('WF40','Change a bundle and review parish readiness','Authorized parish/diocese owner opens manual bundle change or readiness dashboard.','Current/proposed feature matrix, sponsorship, approver, open cases/balances/releases, effect date and manual billing terms if real.','Requested > Impact reviewed > Sponsor approved if required > Effective > Existing work completed > Reviewed','Priest/parish requester;Office/domain owners;Authorized diocesan sponsor;Bundle operator;Case owners;Product/domain reviewer','Manual launch baseline; no invented prices/charges. New write eligibility separate from existing case-completion and history access.','Parish priest or authorized diocesan sponsor; product owners approve matrix.','Downgrade never hides unpaid registrations or awaiting-release documents. Reactivation restores configured module, not revoked record permissions. Unavailable actions show real office route.','Audited plan/effect, protected history and assigned completion paths for every in-flight item.','S29 S32'),
('WF41','Count, independently verify and close giving','Authorized counter opens uniquely identified collection/currency/method batch.','Actual USD/LBP lines, denominations where used, envelope/fund allocations, both counter observations, variance and closing revision.','Opened > First count recorded > Independent second count > Variance resolved > Closed and posted','Counter 1;Counter 1;Distinct eligible counter 2;Both/recount reviewer;Authorized closer','Independent person reviews exact revision; matching totals plus attribution; closure posts each movement once. No fixed sample second-count success.','Treasurer/counting lead; independent counter.','Variance holds batch open. If second person unavailable, remain Unverified and arrange real dual review; any exception requires explicit finance policy, never fake confirmation.','Locked closing snapshot, actual currency/method totals and uniquely posted movements.','S24'),
('WF42','Correct closed giving attribution or amount','Finance operator selects Correct on a closed contribution/count.','Original receipt, reason, corrected allocation or reversal/replacement, independent approver and affected statement.','Correction proposed > Independently approved > Adjustment posted > Statement impact reviewed > Closed','Finance operator;Distinct finance approver;Ledger service;Statement reviewer;Reviewer','Fund/donor reclassification does not create new cash. Wrong currency/amount reverses original then posts actual replacement. Original history retained.','Finance correction approver and treasurer.','No donor visible to unauthorized roles. Failed bank receipt reduces actuals through reversal. Already-issued statements receive linked corrected issue, not silent overwrite.','Net cash changes only for real amount reversal/replacement; attribution and statements trace exact source.','S24 S25'),
('WF43','Request, approve and record an expense','Eligible requester opens expense/purchase/reimbursement.','Purpose/fund/payee, invoice versus actual receipt, currency/amount, evidence, budget and approver.','Draft > Submitted > Approved > Actual payment recorded > Reconciled > Closed','Requester;Requester;Independent finance approver;Authorized payer/recorder;Reconciler;Period reviewer','No self-approval; all nontrivial approvals use named eligible reviewer. No unapproved amount threshold inferred from UI; invoice is liability/evidence, not automatic payment.','Head priest/finance lead; designated independent approver.','Return/decline with reason; missing receipt exception explicitly approved. Cancel approval without pretending paid outflow disappeared; paid correction via reversal.','Actual outflow once, approval/evidence linked and reviewed financial period.','S25'),
('WF44','Reconcile bank movements and close a period','Finance reconciler imports statement or selects unreconciled verified bank lines.','Statement ID/coverage, original currency lines, canonical transactions, split/combined allocations, fees and exceptions.','Imported > Matches proposed > Differences resolved > Independently reviewed > Reconciled > Period closed','Importer;Reconciler;Finance operator;Independent reviewer;Reconciler;Period owner','One statement line cannot be matched twice; allocations reconcile original amounts; explain every difference and source coverage.','Finance reconciler plus independent reviewer.','Duplicates quarantined; unmatched remains open. Undo match before close logs reason; post-close correction needs approved reopen or next-period adjustment, preserving original close.','Statement opening + actual net movements = closing per currency, with exact reconciliation snapshot.','S25'),
('WF45','Operate the separate Office Expenses ledger','Authorized priest/secretary/office administrator records opening balance, allowance or purchase.','Actual currency/date/amount, ledger entry type, source-transfer reference, payee/purpose, receipt/voucher and review period.','Draft > Recorded > Evidence reviewed > Monthly reviewed > Locked > Adjustment if needed','Office operator;Office operator;Office reviewer;Independent finance/priest reviewer;Period service;Authorized reviewer','One initial opening balance per currency; subsequent carry-forward computed. Allowance is an internal transfer pair, purchase recorded once as actual expense.','Office ledger custodian; head priest/finance lead approves close.','Unreviewed edit/delete keeps history; after monthly close use reversal/adjustment. Negative balance flags investigation, not invented money. Receipts retain approved access/retention.','USD/LBP separate rolling balances and internal vouchers reconcile to canonical transfer/payment references.','S25'),
('WF46','Send private conversations and operational notifications','Permitted sender opens Inbox/request conversation or authorized audience compose.','Exact recipients/audience, actual sender/capacity, language, subject/body, permitted files and channel availability.','Draft > Audience preview > Sent in-app > Recipient opened > Archived in own view','Sender;Sender;Messaging service;Recipient;Participant','No public people enumeration; recipient permission checked at send/read; request thread is canonical in timeline and Inbox. External delivery requires evidence.','Sender/authorized shared-office handlers; delivery owner handles failures.','Correction adds follow-up; ordinary sent message not edited/deleted. New participant cannot silently read earlier thread; default starts new thread or explicitly approved forward.','Stored conversation for permitted recipients, separate sent/delivered/read facts and per-user archive.','S26'),
('WF47','Submit and independently review a confidential concern','Authenticated eligible account selects Concerns & complaints and informed identified/reviewer-anonymous route.','Category/urgency, narrative/evidence, eligible selected reviewers, optional identified details, access grants and conflict declaration.','Submitted > Independent assignment > Accepted > Under review > Response provided > Closed > Reopened','Submitter;Conflict-free authority;Reviewer;Reviewer;Reviewer;Reviewer;Conflict-free reviewer','Selected case scope plus Review/ViewSensitive/ViewIdentity as required; no case/count for unrelated admins. Reviewer anonymity is not infrastructure noncorrelation.','Preappointed independent conflict-free concern authority; actual names/contact must be supplied.','All reviewers conflicted stops routing and shows maintained independent contact. Recusal reassigns without broad office exposure. Leaving parish preserves own tracking; cases are not inherited by title.','Restricted case history/replies and review outcome, with applicant-only view and minimal notifications.','S27'),
('WF48','Write private pastoral notes and share a task','Priest author opens Private pastoral notes or an author-owned task.','Original text, optional permitted person reference, audience, task assignee/due/status, explicit share and restricted attachments.','Author-private draft > Saved private > Explicitly shared if chosen > Task completed > Archived','Author;Author;Author;Permitted assignee;Author','Assignment requires task-specific share; current-priests audience includes future appointees only if author explicitly chooses/explains that audience; no successor/admin browse.','Author and explicit permitted assignee.','Sharing withdrawal ends future access but cannot undo reading. Author after departure gets proposed restricted own archived notebook, not live parish person access; policy approval required.','Author/private snapshot and explicit sharing history; task completion never shares other notes.','S28'),
('WF49','Define, publish, run and revise a custom workflow','Authorized process owner opens Forms & workflows then definition or Start run.','Versioned form/steps, field audiences, assignees, prerequisites, conditional branches, parallel approvals, deadlines and final outcome.','Definition draft > Published version > Run submitted > Steps in progress > Final step completed > Run closed','Process owner;Publisher;Eligible applicant;Assigned step actors;Eligible final actor;Workflow service','Template validation prevents unreachable/unauthorized steps. Hard-coded sacrament controls cannot be weakened by builder. Final step closes only after prerequisites and result commit.','Process owner; current step assignee.','Pause blocks new runs by default, existing runs continue; safety stop separately freezes actions. Runs pin version; migration/reopen/cancel preserves prior steps and resource/money consequences.','Traceable run outcome with version and every actor/time; no false scheduled escalation if runner missing.','S28'),
('WF50','Review access/correction/closure/deletion and retention','Verified subject/representative submits a data request; retention owner reviews a record-class expiry queue.','Requester proof, exact scope/purpose, linked minors/households/official/financial/case data, hold, decision and disclosure/redaction.','Received > Identity reviewed > Dependencies classified > Domain approved > Action executed > Outcome delivered','Requester;Identity reviewer;Records owner;Competent domain approver;Authorized operator;Records owner','No invented retention periods/legal duties. Holds override purge; third-party/private fields redacted; closure and official-record deletion are separate.','Records/privacy owner with clergy/finance/independent safeguarding authorities by class.','Some records retained with explained limited decision; mistaken deletion request can be withdrawn before execution. Suppression/restriction used pending real retention schedule.','Scoped documented response, legitimate retained links and minimal deletion/disclosure proof.','S32'),
('WF51','Discover a parish and published times','Visitor opens directory, Find a Mass, parish profile or public event.','Public names/localities, optional filters/date/time/language, verified coordinates and approved schedule exceptions.','Directory > Filtered results > Parish/event detail > Contact or request start','Visitor;Visitor;Visitor;Visitor','Only participating published parishes. Location permission user-initiated; unknown schedules never imply no Mass; map hidden until real provider.','Parish public-information owner.','Denied location keeps manual search. Missing coordinates excluded from radius result or separate unavailable group. Back restores permitted filters; no tracking/private tokens in shares.','Correct parish identified with honest times/contact and stable public URL in chosen language.','S04'),
('WF52','Enter combined home and change acting context','Account signs in or selects an authorized role/parish filter from the header.','Actual grants/relationships, selected acting capacity, one combined home, per-tab target, preferences and saved permitted drafts.','Authenticated > Role chosen if multiple > Combined home > Context change reviewed > Permitted destination','Identity service;User;Shell;User;Shell','One working role enters directly. Multiple roles require deliberate choice; no automatic last-role bypass. Combined browse labels parish; every mutation has exactly one target and eligible role.','Account holder; appointing authority controls grants.','Save/Discard/Stay before switch; clear selected records/confirmations. Revocation removes next protected read/write and stale counts. No extra personal-home selector.','Acting context unmistakable, no cross-parish mutation or inherited private-record visibility.','S03'),
('WF53','Request and fulfill a Mass intention','Applicant selects Mass intention on one parish or office records call.','Intention as supplied, private/public approved wording, preferred Mass/date, contact, actual offering if any.','Received > Priest reviewed > Mass/date confirmed > Intention included > Completed','Office;Assigned priest;Scheduling owner;Service coordinator;Assigned priest/office','Offering is separate from acceptance; no automatic public family name; Mass availability and approved intention policy supplied by clergy.','Responsible priest and Mass coordinator.','Unavailable date offers alternatives; cancellation/refund separate. Never imply payment caused spiritual approval or a scheduled intention proves ceremony occurred.','Actual intention arrangement/outcome with only approved public text.','S13'),
('WF54','Arrange a house blessing','Requester/representative selects House blessing and provides minimum logistics.','Authorized contact, address, availability, people needed, accessibility/logistics and private notes.','Received > Priest accepted > Visit confirmed > Visit occurred > Completed','Office;Assigned priest;Scheduler;Assigned clergy;Office/clergy','Only designated clergy/necessary coordinator see residential details; requested time remains preference until confirmed.','Assigned priest; visit coordinator.','Unreachable contact/inaccessible time seeks clarification; reschedule updates calendar/resources; no public address from event.','Actual visit completion or reasoned cancellation, minimal retained private logistics.','S13'),
('WF55','Arrange a sick/home visit','Requester/authorized representative selects Sick visit with real urgent pastoral contact alongside form.','Person/contact authority, location, preferred time, urgent flag and strictly necessary privately supplied care/logistics.','Received > Private clergy triage > Accepted > Visit confirmed > Actual outcome recorded > Closed','Office minimal intake;Assigned priest;Assigned priest;Scheduler;Assigned clergy;Clergy','Sensitive health narrative restricted; online queue does not promise immediate help. Actual staffed contact/hours supplied before advertising urgent availability.','Duty/assigned priest and maintained pastoral contact owner.','No request-based diagnosis. Clarify authority privately; unavailable urgent contact uses published availability rather than invented dispatch.','Actual contact/visit result and restricted pastoral record, without ordinary office medical exposure.','S13'),
('WF56','Arrange a priest appointment','Applicant selects Appointment, enters broad topic and time preferences.','Requester/contact, broad topic, preferred slots, participant authority, location/channel and privacy.','Received > Priest reviewed > Time offered > Applicant accepted > Confirmed > Occurred or cancelled','Office minimal intake;Assigned priest;Scheduler;Applicant;Scheduler;Assigned priest','No sensitive confession/pastoral narrative required in ordinary form; exact confirmed clergy/room availability checked.','Priest scheduler and assigned priest.','Slot changes after offer require recheck; decline/reoffer records history; appointment acceptance creates one restricted occurrence, never public subject.','Confirmed appointment and actual outcome, distinct from a submitted preferred date.','S13'),
('WF57','Approve and pay a refund','Eligible payer/office requests refund after participant/booking/correction event.','Original canonical receipt/allocations, reason, approved terms, due amount/currency, payee authority and payment proof.','Requested > Entitlement reviewed > Independently approved > Refund paid > Source allocation adjusted > Closed','Payer/office;Finance reviewer;Distinct approver;Authorized payer;Ledger service;Finance reviewer','Cancellation is not payment. Refund cannot exceed original net receipt allocation; convert only with explicit approved original/refund currency/rate basis.','Finance refund approver and payer.','Decline/partial decision gives explanation. Failed payment remains Approved/unpaid; retries use same operation ID. Preserve transport/deposit allocation separately.','Actual negative movement once, remaining credit/balance and corrected source receipt/statement linkage.','S21 S23 S25'),
('WF58','Verify pickup, independent exit and reconcile paper fallback','Authorized event pickup operator opens active participant session or dated manual roster.','Approved collectors/restrictions, actual verified identity, code as supporting check, independent-exit authorization, time and operator.','Checked in > Collector checked > Pickup authorized > Checked out > Paper reconciliation reviewed if used','Operator;Pickup-authorized operator;Pickup operator or safeguarding lead;Pickup operator;Independent event reviewer','Code alone insufficient; restricted collector has no routine release override. Unknown/outdated authority requires named safeguarding lead/verified guardian under actual parish procedure.','Named safeguarding/event lead, with real contact and trained operators.','Offline use protected roster/paper log; no verified authority means do not release through ordinary flow. Later reconcile original times/source separately from entry time; no duplicate checkout.','Actual recipient/exit basis and time recorded, participant removed from event present-roster exactly once.','S22'),
('WF59','Track pledges and standing expected gifts','Donor/authorized finance user records a promise or expected recurring gift.','Donor authority, amount/currency, fund, frequency/dates, consent to actual reminders and linked receipts.','Draft > Agreed expectation > Active > Receipts allocated > Fulfilled or ended','Finance recorder;Donor/finance reviewer;Finance owner;Allocator;Finance owner','Promise never increases cash balance. No processor means no automatic collection; every receipt is separately verified and posted.','Finance pledge owner; donor controls optional reminders.','Missed due dates create follow-up only. End stops future expectation, preserves receipts. Currency conversion only on real allocation basis.','Expected versus actual separately reported with dated allocations and no fabricated recurring payments.','S24'),
('WF60','Create and close a giving campaign','Approved priest/finance campaign owner creates appeal.','Purpose/restricted fund, genuine target/currency/date, public translations, approved use of excess and eligible receipt allocations.','Draft > Purpose/fund approved > Published > Receiving > Closed > Final report reviewed','Campaign owner;Priest/finance approver;Content publisher;Finance operator;Campaign owner;Independent reviewer','Only actual net received posted gifts affect received progress; pledges separate; no public donor identity without separate consent/authority.','Head priest/finance lead; public publisher.','Restricted/excess funds stay under actual approved rules; no invented redistribution. Closing campaign does not erase outstanding pledge or reverse gifts.','Reconciled actual-by-currency campaign result and permitted public summary.','S24'),
('WF61','Issue contribution receipts and household statements','Permitted finance user selects actual receipt or annual statement for an authorized subject.','Canonical transactions, household attribution at receipt dates, permitted recipient, period/currency, issuance revision and correction reason.','Prepared > Scope reviewed > Approved > Issued > Delivered or collected > Corrected issue if needed','Finance preparer;Finance reviewer;Authorized finance approver;Finance issuer;Verified recipient;Finance reviewer','Household membership not statement access; original currencies distinct; no unsupported tax-validity wording; print language reviewed.','Finance document owner.','Wrong donor/fund/amount uses WF42; new statement links superseded issue. Delivery availability is not receipt; undelivered artifact remains in follow-up.','Versioned accurate receipt/statement, original transaction IDs and authorized recipient evidence.','S24'),
('WF62','Submit, review and withdraw a prayer intention','Account or permitted guest opens Prayer intention and chooses clergy-private/anonymous-public/named-public.','Supplied wording, subject representation, audience choice, proposed public redaction, translation and publication permission.','Submitted private > Clergy/content reviewed > Approved wording > Published if chosen > Withdrawn or expired','Submitter;Eligible clergy/publisher;Submitter and publisher;Publisher;Submitter/publisher','Private is default; third-party/private health details redacted; public named content needs actual approved authority; prayer submission never joins mailing list.','Designated priest/prayer publisher.','Return unsuitable wording with useful explanation; withdrawal ends future distribution, cannot recall printed copies. External delivery not implied.','Private handling or exact approved public revision, with retained minimal publication/withdrawal history.','S26'),
('WF63','Keep personal member notes','Signed-in account opens My notes in permitted personal area of combined home.',"Author's original title/body, optional private tags, created/updated times and attachment choices.",'Draft > Saved private > Edited > Archived > Deleted if retention permits','Author;Author;Author;Author;Author/retention service','Account-private, never ordinary office/group/clergy feed. No other household adult or staff role inherits it.','Account author; platform support cannot browse notebook.','Sign-out clears shared-device sensitive recovery. Conflicts preserve authorized draft. Trash/erase only under approved personal-data schedule, distinct from pastoral/official records.','Private note persisted only for author, with no accidental staff projection.','S28'),
('WF64','Export permitted data or create an actual backup','Authorized user selects selected/all-matching export; authorized operator separately invokes documented infrastructure backup procedure.','Scope/purpose/columns/date/language, restricted exclusions, snapshot time and actual backup coverage/restore evidence.','Requested > Scope previewed > Authorized > Generated > Downloaded > Audited','User;User;Export service;Export service;User;Audit service','Export authorization beyond view for sensitive/bulk fields; filters/count fixed. Data snapshot is not restorable backup; only operators handle actual backup/restore controls.','Data export owner; separate technical backup custodian.','Role revocation before retrieval blocks export. Partial export reports omitted records; no silent current-page limit. Backup readiness requires real restore exercise, not documentation claim.','Correct field-limited artifact or explicitly evidenced restorable backup, never conflated.','S31 S32'),
('WF65','Approve formation milestones','Assigned instructor/leader opens an eligible member milestone on a defined formation program.','Program/version, milestones/prerequisites, evidence, attendance where relevant, reviewer and actual completion date.','Enrolled > In progress > Evidence submitted > Reviewed > Completed or returned','Instructor;Learner/instructor;Instructor;Designated qualified reviewer;Reviewer','Actual clergy approval where required; attendance alone not automatic spiritual eligibility; external evidence reviewed rather than duplicated course.','Formation coordinator and designated priest/qualified reviewer.','Missing evidence returns milestone only; changed program pins version or reviewed migration. Course certificate is not sacramental certificate.','Verified program milestone history and clearly labeled formation output.','S19'),
